  Statement of the Problem

  The bus error is not caused by a logical flaw in your C application code. The fixes applied have already made the code robust against the most
  common memory management errors.

  The problem lies in a lower-level, latent bug within one of the C libraries being used—most likely json-glib or libsoup. The specific data stream
  being sent back by the llama3 model from Ollama, even when handled correctly by your application code, is triggering a fatal memory-handling error
  (a bus error, likely from a misaligned memory access) deep inside one of these underlying libraries as it parses the raw HTTP response. Your
  application code is correct, but the library it is calling cannot handle the specific data it is being fed.
